   "why": "silhouette IoU is computed from binary masks of projected geometry only. No material, no permittivity, no conductivity, no frequency, no polarisation and no scattering integral enters it. The RCS comparison (level and slope) enters through material-weighted physical optics on the same mesh. The two tests share the mesh and nothing else, so they are two independent pieces of evidence about the same object.",
