  "where": "src/viz_mesh_photo.py",
  "what": "mesh_parts() stores each propeller's sampled points in propeller-local coordinates (centred on the origin) and keeps the rotor position separately in part['center']. Every consumer — Fitter.__init__, final_masks(), clipped_fraction() — projects p['P'] - centre and never adds part['center'] back. spin() then rotates that origin-centred cloud about the rotor position, which translates the propeller around a circle of radius |rotor centre| instead of spinning it about its own shaft.",
